[ledge] Wrong assumed print direction for this factory tool. Its documented common Y79.515 back lies on the bed after a +90° X rotation, building along machine +Y. These Z-normal bridge faces are vertical in that pose. magnet-geometry.json/factory_gauges binds the actual STL and finds zero horizontal undersides above the bed.
alternatives: Printing in machine +Z requires bridge-arm supports. The flat-back pose starts the central rib, feet and bridge on one bed plane while preserving the 1.750 mm pole-setting step. No machine-frame geometry change is needed.
