[thin] Numerical threshold boundary at the complete nominal 3 mm tool plate. Its actual native planes are Y79.515 and Y82.515, and the corresponding STL interval and extended analytic chord both measure 3.000 mm. magnet-geometry.json/factory_gauges and dock-lint-review.json bind both surfaces. This diagnoses the threshold without claiming printed gauge accuracy.
alternatives: Thickening an already nominal 3 mm plate only to pass the floating-point ranking changes the factory tool without correcting a smaller designed section. Distinguish the numerical boundary and measure the finished registering step separately.
